WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.368
We do have a representative

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:03.269
from Tennessee, Jerry Faison.

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.004
He is the Tennessee

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:06.072
Republican caucus chair joining us now.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.241
And good evening. Thanks for joining us.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.143
Can you just kind of explain to us

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.812
why you believe these two members

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:16.049
have just been expelled?

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:18.818
Thank you. That that's a great question.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:19.686
First of all, I'd like to say

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.988
this is a terribly sad time.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.257
This is a very grave situation

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:27.293
that someone would be expelled.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.461
Before that,

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.196
we've had some serious tragedies

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:30.864
in Tennessee.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:33.033
And the six innocent lives

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.667
that were lost last week

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.503
are are absolutely devastating.

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:36.970
So

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.073
I want to make sure that we mention that

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:40.840
that that's

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:41.975
one of the biggest things going on

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.143
right now in Tennessee.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:45.111
You asked me specifically about

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.713
why do I think they should be expelled?

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:47.847
I think that's a great question.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.649
America deserves to know.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:50.950
We have several hundred years

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.720
over 200 years of of of

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.522
of an incredible state,

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:56.823
incredible state house history.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:57.791
That's rich

00:00:57.791 --> 00:00:58.258
Tennessee

00:00:58.258 --> 00:00:59.459
is one of the most important states

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.061
in all of America.

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.862
We have had literally thousands

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:04.197
of state reps

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:07.434
since 1796 who have who have worked.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.769
And then after 1859 have worked

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:10.637
in this very chamber

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.672
that you're seeing me in today.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.941
They have all understood

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:15.842
that there are rules

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.911
and procedures to ensure

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.046
that every voice is heard.

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:22.315
There's almost 7 million Tennesseans,

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.150
and we have come up with these ideas

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.418
that the best way

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.420
for everybody to be heard

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.254
is to make sure

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:30.557
that we follow the rules of decorum.

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:32.559
So these members have come

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.761
in this entire. Go ahead.

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:36.396
Let me just representative there

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:39.199
interrupt to say I understand decorum.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.433
Van was just making the point there.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:40.800
Of course,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.334
not everyone

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.569
can bring a bullhorn in every time

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:43.169
they disagreed.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.604
Otherwise it would be total chaos.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:45.839
But why take this step?

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:46.739
Why was there

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.708
no measure you could have taken

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.510
before this, before expulsion?

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.712
Why take the most extreme step

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:55.348
so quickly?

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.617
So that's an excellent question.

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:58.351
More than just

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.853
what America has seen

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:01.521
that took place last Thursday,

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.156
there is a history

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:05.358
all year long of disrupting

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:08.161
committees and the House floor

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:10.463
getting off of the germane topic.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:11.097
When I say germane,

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:11.965
that is what we're dealing

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.032
with at that moment.

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.434
Just to make political grandstand,

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.568
we've called them out.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:16.603
The chairmen of committees,

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:17.303
the speaker of the House

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.872
have been calling them out,

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:21.674
Tom and Tom again for grabbing the mic,

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:23.243
sucking the air out of the room,

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:25.278
making sure no other voices heard.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.147
And finally, when they come

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.781
and and act

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.650
so foolish on the House floor,

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.784
this is a sacred place

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.153
that belongs to everybody

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.220
and literally start

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.055
looking up into the gallery

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:37.157
with a bullhorn,

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:38.825
getting the protesters

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:40.793
worked up into a frenzy.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.862
That is incumbent on us to say

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:44.964
you've gone a step too far

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:47.200
and we're going to take steps

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.268
to make sure

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:49.969
that if you ever do come back,

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.171
if you get reelected,

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.705
that, you know, it's a serious thing

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:53.706
to Tennesseans

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.108
that you come and disrupt

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.142
the people's house.

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:57.744
So I think it was very,

00:02:57.744 --> 00:02:59.445
very important for us to do that.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:00.213
The speaker here

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.848
likened what they did

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.449
to what happened on January six

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.584
in Washington, D.C..

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:07.620
Do you agree with that comparison?

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.589
I believe them coming in

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:11.124
and taking over the house.

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:13.293
They called it occupying the well.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:13.927
The where's

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:15.328
the well is where we send up front

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.163
to pass our bills.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.298
That that is

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:20.533
that is incredibly disruptive

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:21.401
and embarrassing

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:22.268
to the legislature,

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:24.571
the institution that we have here.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:27.540
And I didn't see anybody in Congress

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.209
try to take over.

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:31.578
Now, I saw some really big idiots

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:32.912
that I hope are punished

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.214
to the full extent of the law.

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:35.481
Come and break into the Capitol

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.550
and act foolish on January six.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.719
But I didn't see a congressman act

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:40.453
this way.

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:41.955
What we saw here in Tennessee

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:44.023
is three elected state representatives

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.358
who know the rules,

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:45.925
who understand

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.560
that this place belongs to everybody.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.429
They come in and rush up here

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:51.497
and take over the House floor and refuse.

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.366
Even when our sergeant arms.

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:54.234
He's a gentle soul.

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:55.935
Several of them are just great men.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:57.637
Come and gently encourage them.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.038
Gus, not right now.

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:00.240
Listen, don't do this.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:00.940
I mean, they told.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.141
They sent them away.

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:04.143
It was. It was.

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:06.746
It's an embarrassment to everybody

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.781
to see someone come and behave like that.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.216
And good, gentle souls

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:10.883
who are sergeant

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.452
arms have been here for years.

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:13.753
Come in and try to encourage you.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.822
Hey, you're making a mistake.

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:16.623
And they didn't do it.

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:18.958
And I'd like to add to your

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:20.193
they they've not backed down

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:21.661
from that either.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:21.928
You know,

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:24.230
I told them earlier that I feel like

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:25.598
if they would have said, you know what,

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.301
we messed up.

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:30.303
I mean, what American wouldn't

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:34.007
Tuman bring forgiveness and redemption.

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:35.541
But they doubled down

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.176
and went so far as to stain in the world

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:39.212
today and said I'd do it again.

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:40.680
That was their mentality.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.848
That shows me

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:42.315
when there's

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:44.083
a pattern of behavior like that.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:46.419
If you refuse to stop it yourself,

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:47.987
then we have to step in

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.455
as a group of individuals

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:50.523
that work with you and say

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:51.524
you're not do that here.

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:51.758
Well,

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:52.825
they said they were passionate

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.661
because of the underlying reason

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:55.662
that I think is important here

00:04:55.662 --> 00:04:56.496
to also remind people,

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:58.431
which is because six people were killed

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:59.499
in a shooting last week.

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:01.801
And just on your point on January six,

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:02.235
the reason the

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.102
Congress that we're doing this,

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:04.270
because they were being evacuated,

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:05.405
because the insurrectionists

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:07.040
were taking over the Capitol.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.308
But I do want my colleague

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:09.275
here, Van Jones,

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:10.443
he also has a question for you.

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:10.810
And thank you

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:11.811
again for being here tonight.

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:14.614
Thank you for for joining us.

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:16.416
I just wonder,

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:19.285
there are people who are members

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.219
of that state legislature.

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:22.221
And by the way, I work for a gymnasium.

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:22.989
Speaker Nancy,

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:24.891
I got my start in the state legislature.

00:05:24.891 --> 00:05:26.793
So it's a friend, exactly.

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:27.660
One of the best ever.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.828
And I'm from from Madison County,

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:29.629
born in Jackson, Tennessee.

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:31.397
So so I know how things work

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:32.465
in that state legislature.

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:34.067
And you have an array of tools

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.969
as a leader to get people to comply.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.505
Why did you not go to the Ethics

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:39.872
Committee?

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:43.242
Why did you not go through due process?

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:46.045
If you are here saying you want

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:48.614
this legislator to be respected.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.383
Why are you not following the rules

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:52.118
and using the tools that you have?

00:05:52.118 --> 00:05:53.686
You want them to not be extreme,

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:55.121
but you're being extreme. Why is that?

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:55.922
Our democracy.

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.257
So a lot of

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:59.959
accusation on your part there.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:01.494
We actually are following the rules

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:03.663
and we gave them ample chance.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.231
We established

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:07.233
what was taking place on Monday.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:08.968
There was due process.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.536
Did you go make it?

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:11.771
It's not just up to me.

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:13.973
There's there's actually,

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:15.808
you know, of 71,

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:16.209
I think, or

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:19.212
70 of the members who after looking at

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:22.248
what took place today, they voted two

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:25.785
to expel one of them, one in 69

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:26.753
from that committee.

00:06:26.753 --> 00:06:27.453
And just try to understand,

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:28.221
why did you not go to

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:29.222
the Ethics Committee

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:30.423
and do the things

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:32.058
that are always done in that body?

00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:33.793
You have not done this to anybody

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:35.628
except for two people in 200 years.

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:36.729
You can't tell me that

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:37.630
there have not been people

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:38.831
who have also been disrupted,

00:06:38.831 --> 00:06:39.198
that you've had

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:41.067
people have peed on chairs

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:42.301
that did not get expelled.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:43.069
So I don't understand

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:44.937
why you skipped the Ethics Committee.

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:46.873
If you want respect

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:48.040
and if you want

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.742
for people to be reasonable,

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.210
why are you being so unreasonable

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.178
and why are you skipping steps?

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:53.012
I don't understand.

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:54.414
You seem to be contradicting.

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:55.915
You're not acting the way you want.

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:58.518
The young people act.

00:06:58.518 --> 00:07:01.254
So the story of someone urinated on

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:01.521
some of somebody's

00:07:01.521 --> 00:07:03.489
stairs is never been quantified.

00:07:03.489 --> 00:07:04.991
I've heard many people say

00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:05.658
they don't think there's

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:06.726
any truth to that.

00:07:06.726 --> 00:07:08.261
So what you need to understand is

00:07:08.261 --> 00:07:10.496
this is a body of people

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.632
who decide corporately

00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:14.333
what we're going to do moving forward.

00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:17.470
This body spoke many times.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:18.905
I brought our caucus together

00:07:18.905 --> 00:07:21.007
several times since last Thursday

00:07:21.007 --> 00:07:24.210
to ask the body what we as a group

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.411
wanted to do.

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:27.480
The overwhelming majority,

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.981
the heartbeat of this caucus

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:31.884
is not on this House floor, not this way.

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:34.587
So if there was an idea of

00:07:34.587 --> 00:07:36.122
send it to the ethics group,

00:07:36.122 --> 00:07:37.457
this group, my caucus,

00:07:37.457 --> 00:07:38.658
which is the super majority

00:07:38.658 --> 00:07:40.593
there, 75 of us said, no,

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:41.160
that is not

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.628
we don't want to go to the ethics rep.

00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:43.830
We don't want them censured.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.264
We want them expelled.

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:46.799
So when you're in leadership,

00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:48.134
you encourage people

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:50.002
to look at all the aspects

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:51.137
and then you work with what

00:07:51.137 --> 00:07:52.505
the majority of your people want to do.

00:07:52.505 --> 00:07:53.739
And that's exactly what we did.

00:07:54.841 --> 00:07:56.909
Sara Sara Sidner, I had a question.

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:58.110
You mentioned

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:00.313
that you thought that the representatives

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:02.281
were riling up the crowd.

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:03.483
And I can tell you from the reporters

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:04.050
that were out there,

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.384
the crowd was already riled up.

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:07.353
They are extremely upset

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:09.422
that your legislature

00:08:09.422 --> 00:08:11.958
wasn't trying to deal with the issue

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:14.393
of keeping children safe in school,

00:08:14.393 --> 00:08:15.528
but instead

00:08:15.528 --> 00:08:17.663
going after these two Democrats.

00:08:17.663 --> 00:08:20.299
And I wonder, sir, who are you punishing?

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:20.967
Because, yes,

00:08:20.967 --> 00:08:23.169
you have kicked out these two Democrats,

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:24.303
but there are tens

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:25.771
of thousands of constituents

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:27.073
that are also being punished

00:08:27.073 --> 00:08:28.841
and don't have any representation

00:08:28.841 --> 00:08:29.342
right now.

00:08:29.342 --> 00:08:31.944
What do you say to them?

00:08:32.111 --> 00:08:33.212
So, first of all,

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:35.314
the censure, the part that you said

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:36.015
you didn't think

00:08:36.015 --> 00:08:37.717
the crowd was already worked up,

00:08:37.717 --> 00:08:39.085
so they weren't working up.

00:08:39.085 --> 00:08:41.420
I'd like you to go back and watch.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.122
Watch what took place today.

00:08:43.122 --> 00:08:45.124
They literally control the crowd.

00:08:45.124 --> 00:08:46.726
They control the protesters.

00:08:46.726 --> 00:08:47.393
They look at them.

00:08:47.393 --> 00:08:48.227
They do their hand like this.

00:08:48.227 --> 00:08:49.328
They do their hand like this.

00:08:49.328 --> 00:08:51.063
It's like leading the choir.

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:52.932
So the notion that you think

00:08:52.932 --> 00:08:53.699
that they weren't

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:56.068
getting the people incited

00:08:56.068 --> 00:08:57.570
and worked up into a frenzy,

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:58.504
unfortunately weren't here.

00:08:58.504 --> 00:08:59.105
You didn't see it.

00:08:59.105 --> 00:09:00.573
That's exactly what they did.

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:01.741
And they protest today.

00:09:01.741 --> 00:09:02.909
But stand up and tell them

00:09:02.909 --> 00:09:03.843
they talked to some of them

00:09:03.843 --> 00:09:05.311
and some of them were teachers

00:09:05.311 --> 00:09:06.646
who were so distraught

00:09:06.646 --> 00:09:07.880
they were near tears

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.315
because they could not believe

00:09:09.315 --> 00:09:10.883
that their lawmakers

00:09:10.883 --> 00:09:11.784
were doing this

00:09:11.784 --> 00:09:12.885
as opposed to dealing

00:09:12.885 --> 00:09:15.087
with the biggest issue at hand.

00:09:15.087 --> 00:09:15.922
The number one

00:09:15.922 --> 00:09:18.291
killer of children is gun violence,

00:09:18.291 --> 00:09:19.158
and they wanted you

00:09:19.158 --> 00:09:20.626
all to do something about that

00:09:20.626 --> 00:09:22.662
instead of wasting time and their mind

00:09:22.995 --> 00:09:24.063
when it comes to this.

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:24.664
I mean, they literally

00:09:24.664 --> 00:09:25.765
talked about it on the air.

00:09:25.765 --> 00:09:27.400
So they were already quite worked up

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:29.135
because they love their state

00:09:29.135 --> 00:09:30.770
and they love their kids

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:31.537
and they want to

00:09:31.537 --> 00:09:34.473
see a safer place for the children

00:09:35.308 --> 00:09:36.809
and themselves, really.

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:39.812
So I'm sure that's what you think.

00:09:39.812 --> 00:09:41.347
But we watched them

00:09:41.347 --> 00:09:42.982
today, directed them

00:09:42.982 --> 00:09:44.784
like a choir leader would.

00:09:44.784 --> 00:09:46.118
That was what was amazing.

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:47.420
And I'll tell you this

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:48.921
and unfortunately, I've got to go.

00:09:48.921 --> 00:09:50.823
I'm I'm three and a half hours from home.

00:09:50.823 --> 00:09:51.991
Compelling argument

00:09:51.991 --> 00:09:53.593
I think you've reached an

00:09:53.593 --> 00:09:56.729
it's not possible for us to move forward

00:09:57.396 --> 00:09:57.997
with the way

00:09:57.997 --> 00:09:59.432
they were behaving in committee

00:09:59.432 --> 00:10:00.766
and on the House floor.

00:10:00.766 --> 00:10:02.835
There's got to be some peace.

00:10:02.835 --> 00:10:03.569
And for them,

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:05.137
the way they were behaving

00:10:05.137 --> 00:10:07.106
to disrupt every committee, disrupt

00:10:07.106 --> 00:10:08.341
the House floor, they were.

00:10:08.341 --> 00:10:09.942
How can we get to the

00:10:09.942 --> 00:10:11.210
to the answers of

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:11.978
what are we going to do

00:10:11.978 --> 00:10:13.079
about gun violence?

00:10:13.079 --> 00:10:14.213
What are we going to do

00:10:14.213 --> 00:10:15.114
about guns and college?

00:10:15.114 --> 00:10:16.482
What are we going to do about red flag?

00:10:16.482 --> 00:10:16.782
Well,

00:10:17.016 --> 00:10:19.018
the conversation can't happen

00:10:19.018 --> 00:10:20.152
because they're drowning out,

00:10:20.152 --> 00:10:21.687
sucking all the air out of the room.

00:10:21.687 --> 00:10:23.689
So I would just push back on you saying

00:10:23.689 --> 00:10:24.857
we can't get there

00:10:25.825 --> 00:10:26.826
if they won't let us.

00:10:26.826 --> 00:10:27.426
And thank you

00:10:27.426 --> 00:10:28.427
for letting me speak with you.

00:10:28.427 --> 00:10:29.495
God bless. Representative.

00:10:29.495 --> 00:10:30.029
Representative,

00:10:30.029 --> 00:10:30.963
I know you got a long drive home.

00:10:30.963 --> 00:10:33.432
One final question for you.

00:10:33.766 --> 00:10:34.166
All right.

00:10:34.166 --> 00:10:36.268
Well, Jeremy Faison has left us

00:10:36.268 --> 00:10:38.004
is the Republican chair in Tennessee.

00:10:38.004 --> 00:10:38.471
Of course,

00:10:38.471 --> 00:10:39.271
that was the House

00:10:39.271 --> 00:10:40.740
and voted tonight to expel

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.041
these two Republicans or these

00:10:42.041 --> 00:10:43.109
two Democrats, I should note.

